  "notes": [
    "Data came from the JSON/CSV endpoints the hub itself fetches, saved verbatim in raw.json keyed by URL: /data/benchmarks.json (benchmark metadata), /data/benchmarks.csv (run-level results for Epoch AI's own benchmarks), /data/benchmarked_models.csv (model metadata + Epoch Capabilities Index), /data/external_benchmark_paths.json and the 66 files under /data/external_benchmarks/.",
    "normalized.json holds one record per source row per headline metric. The metric field is the exact column name from the source CSV; no scores were rescaled, so percentage benchmarks are mostly 0-1 fractions while some external leaderboards publish 0-100 or unbounded values (e.g. Arena Score, METR time horizon in minutes, ECI).",
    "Rows from /data/benchmarks.csv are individual evaluation runs, so a model can appear more than once per Epoch AI benchmark; the site aggregates these for display.",
    "date is the model version release date as published by Epoch, not the evaluation date.",
    "cost_usd is only set where the source leaderboard has an explicit cost column (Cost, Cost per task, Cost per run, Cost per test (USD), Total cost (USD), Average costs, Spend, Average cost (USD)); its unit basis differs between benchmarks.",
    "rank is only set where the source provides a rank column (CursorBench, ALE-Bench, ForecastBench). No ranks were computed.",
    "context_window is not published anywhere in this dataset, so the field is omitted from every record.",
    "Fiction.liveBench and GeoBench publish no single overall score, so each of their sub-scores is emitted as its own record with the sub-score column as the metric.",
    "benchmarks.csv also contains Epoch task ids with no public benchmark page (OEIS Open, OEIS Open Lite, FrontierMath-2025-02-28-Public, FrontierMath-Tier-4-2025-07-01-Public, and the new FrontierMath-Erdos); they are included and point at the hub URL.",
    "Model identity resolution tries columns in this order per source row: Model (joined display name), Model version (raw id_model_version), Name, Agent -- some external leaderboards (e.g. GSM8K, OS World, Terminal-Bench) carry the model's identity only in a 'Name' or 'Agent' column when Epoch has not joined the row to its own model registry.",
    "Reproduced the reference scrape's benchmark-to-metric-column mapping by reverse-engineering it from the 20260903 normalized.json (unique benchmark/metric pairs), then re-fetched all 70 endpoints live and re-parsed every CSV rather than reusing old data; a schema-drift guard compares each CSV's header against the expected metric column and falls back to heuristic detection with a logged warning if the expected column is missing (not triggered on this run)."
  ],
